   "widgets_values": [
    "# 360 panorama -> camera views + sheet\n\nTurns a 2:1 equirectangular panorama into normal camera views taken from its centre, turning right from\none view to the next.\n\n- **views**: a batch with one image per view.\n- **sheet**: the same views stacked in one column on a white page. This is the image to give a video\n  model as the location reference.\n\nSettings: `views` (how many around the full turn), `width` / `height` of each view, `h_fov_deg` (field\nof view; wider than 360 / views makes neighbours overlap), `first_yaw_deg` (direction of view 1,\n0 = centre of the panorama), `margin` (white gap on the sheet).\n\nThe detail of a view is the panorama width x h_fov / 360: upscale the panorama first if the views look\nsoft. If the panorama's left and right edges do not match, the view that looks backwards shows the break.\n"
   ],
   "title": "What this does"
  }
